SponsorBlock
------------

`yt_final` can ask yt-dlp to fetch community-submitted segment data from the
SponsorBlock API at https://sponsor.ajay.app and either mark those segments as
chapters or cut them out. This happens only when the user asks for it, via
`--sponsorblock-*`; nothing is contacted otherwise.

This is the one third-party source whose DATA ENDS UP INSIDE FILES THE USER
KEEPS: marked segments are written into the output as chapter titles of the form
`[SponsorBlock]: <category>`. A user who redistributes such a file redistributes
SponsorBlock's contribution with it.

The SponsorBlock database is published by the SponsorBlock project under its own
terms, which include an attribution requirement and, in the versions published
to date, a non-commercial condition. Those terms are the database's, not this
project's, and they are NOT superseded by the root Unlicense. Anyone
redistributing yt_final output that contains SponsorBlock-derived chapters, or
building a commercial product on this tool with the feature enabled, must check
the current licence at https://sponsor.ajay.app and satisfy it themselves.

The exact licence version and the scope of its non-commercial term are part of
the open legal review recorded in requirements/README.md; this notice records the
dependency, and is not a determination that the terms are compatible.

